    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d28">

                <pb facs="0114" n="40" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg40"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1646.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-01-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 4, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I enclose for your information a copy of a
                    despatch, of the 30th of November last, from Mr. Morse, the United States consul
                    at London, and a copy of a letter, of the 20th ultimo, from the Secretary of the
                    Treasury, upon the subject of the recovery of a large amount of gold, alleged to
                    be deposited in England, which was the property of the late insurgent
                    authorities. Mr. Morse has been informed of the opinion of the Secretary of the
                    Treasury.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>




                <xi:include href="d28-a1.xml" xpointer="d28-a1"/>
